  "review_notes": [
    "Each of the four redemption verbs is rendered by the phrase do or perform the part of a kinsman, taken whole with the verb and headed on kinsman; part was the competing head and is named here once for all four.",
    "The prepositions unto and to before the object suffixes are the English verb's valency and belong to the verb's unit (rule 44), the suffixes keeping only thee.",
